From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@smartrg.com>
Date: Thu, 09 Dec 2021 16:21:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: add TRIGGER_ACS to report an ACS pick

An operator needs the channel that ACS picks for a running AP,
without a move of the AP. TRIGGER_ACS (hostapd_cli trigger_acs) runs
ACS on an enabled interface and reports the pick, and the operator
then moves the AP with a channel switch. The CLI and the system log
read the result of every ACS run.

Each successful ACS run writes its pick to /tmp/hapd_acs_<phy>, and
the ACS log lines use MSG_WARNING with the phy name. During a manual
run the AP stays in state ENABLED, and ACS writes its pick into the
configuration in one step at the end. The run saves the channel state
just before that step and restores it right after, so changes from
other events persist. TRIGGER_ACS is refused during a channel switch
or a CAC, with ACS offload, and while a run is active. Control
interface, ubus and ucode switch requests are refused during a run; a
radar switch, a stop or a disable ends it. A busy scan and missing
scan results fail an ACS run only once, because a second failure
report would disable the AP.

Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
